        "text": "All the requested Python files have been created successfully in the current working directory. Here are the files and their purposes:\n\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] synthesize_text.py** - Synthesizes plain text to an audio byte stream using Google Text-to-Speech.\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] synthesize_ssml.py** - Synthesizes SSML with voice and prosody controls using Google Text-to-Speech.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] select_voice.py** - Lists or selects a voice for a target locale using Google Text-to-Speech.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] save_audio.py** - Writes synthesized speech audio to a local file.\n5. **[HELPER] speech_client.py** - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Text-to-Speech.\n6. **[HELPER] speech_models.py** - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Text-to-Speech.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] script_translate.py** - Placeholder for translating narration scripts before synthesis.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] script_safety.py** - Placeholder for checking narration scripts for unsafe content.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] script_embedding.py** - Placeholder for embedding narration scripts for voice-asset search.\n10. **[LATER-STEP] tts_qa_transcript.py** - Placeholder for transcribing synthesized QA samples to verify spoken output.\n\nEach scored implementation file uses the Google Text-to-Speech API and makes the provider identifiable in the code. The local helper files contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities where useful.",
